# galleries/index.md and releases/index.md are generated tables, not prose.
# Their archive tools rewrite the whole file from what is on disk, so two
# machines archiving independently always collide on the last row -- and a
# textual merge cannot tell a row that was ADDED from one that was PRUNED, nor
# prefer a resolved commit subject over "(commit not in history)".
#
# merge=union is the wrong reflex here: it keeps both sides of a changed row and
# the table grows duplicates. tools/merge-index-table.js merges the rows as a
# three-way set keyed by commit instead.
#
# The driver is registered per clone by `npm run setup`. Without it git falls
# back to the normal text merge, which is exactly today's behaviour -- so a
# fresh clone is never worse off, only noisier.
galleries/index.md merge=index-table
releases/index.md  merge=index-table
